    {
      "id": "find-closest-point",
      "name": "FindClosestPoint",
      "category": "SparseDynamicPointOctree3",
      "signature": "FindClosestPoint(Target, Query Pt, Distance Threshold, Predicate Func, Dist Sq Func, Temp Buffer)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FSparseDynamicPointOctree3*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Query Pt",
          "type": "FVector3d"
        },
        {
          "name": "Distance Threshold",
          "type": "Double"
        },
        {
          "name": "Predicate Func",
          "type": "TFunctionRef<bool ( int32 )>"
        },
        {
          "name": "Dist Sq Func",
          "type": "TFunctionRef<double ( int32 )>"
        },
        {
          "name": "Temp Buffer",
          "type": "TArray<FSparsePointOctreeCell*>*",
          "default": "nullptr"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Int",
      "docs": "Find closest point in the tree, relative to a query point, within a search distance\n@param QueryPt Find the point closest to this query point\n@param DistanceThreshold Limit the search to this distance\n@param PredicateFunc Return true if point should be included (i.e., this is a filter)\n@param DistSqFunc User-provided squared distance between the point with the given ID and the QueryPt\n@param TempBuffer Optional temporary buffer to store a queue of cells (to avoid memory allocations)\n@return The ID of the closest point, or INDEX_NONE if no point was found"
    },
    {
      "id": "configure-from-point-count-estimate",
      "name": "ConfigureFromPointCountEstimate",
      "category": "SparseDynamicPointOctree3",
      "signature": "ConfigureFromPointCountEstimate(Target, Max Bounds Dimension, Count Estimate)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FSparseDynamicPointOctree3*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Max Bounds Dimension",
          "type": "Double"
        },
        {
          "name": "Count Estimate",
          "type": "Int"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "FSparseDynamicPointOctree3 sorts Points with axis-aligned bounding boxes into a dynamic\nsparse octree of axis-aligned uniform grid cells. At the top level we have an infinite\ngrid of \"root cells\" of size RootDimension, which then contain 8 children, and so on.\n(So in fact each cell is a separate octree, and we have a uniform grid of octrees)\nThe Points and their bounding-boxes are not stored in the tree. You must have an\ninteger identifier (PointID) for each Point, and call Insert(PointID, BoundingBox).\nSome query functions will require you to provide a lambda/etc that can be called to\nretrieve the bounding box for a given PointID.\nBy default Points are currently inserted at the maximum possible depth, ie smallest cell that\nwill contain them, or MaxTreeDepth.\nThe octree is dynamic. Points can be removed and re-inserted."
    },
